    "result_text": "The build is green. `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class (the other two files are support classes), and it passes along with the full suite.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `bulkSignupWarning` rule for the owner endpoints.\n\n**The rule:** when more than 80 owners already share the same business-day `registrationDate`, the response includes `bulkSignupWarning: true`; otherwise `false`. This mirrors the existing daily-limit accumulation path (`EnsureBelowDailyLimit`, which caps at 100).\n\n**Changes:**\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `bulkSignupWarning` boolean property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it.\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient Boolean bulkSignupWarning` field with getter/setter (transient because it's derived at response time, not persisted). MapStruct maps it onto the DTO by name automatically.\n3. **`EvaluateBulkSignupWarning.java`** \u2014 new function step that counts owners sharing this owner's `registrationDate` and sets the flag to `count > 80`, mutating the entity in place via `@Val`.\n4. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted the step after `audit`, before `respond`, under `transaction` governance, so the create response reflects the warning.\n5. **`owners/{ownerId}.GET.yml`** \u2014 inserted the step between `load` and `respond`, under `readonly-transaction`, so a read-back computes the flag consistently (this is the path the acceptance test exercises).\n\nThe acceptance test creates one owner and reads `$.bulkSignupWarning` back via GET, asserting `false` (under threshold) \u2014 which now passes.",
